WEBVTT

00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:06.194
<i>Yamanashi!</i>

00:00:06.402 --> 00:00:10.114
<i>Good morning, Yamanashi!</i>

00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:13.284
<i>Yamanashi!
Good morning, Yamanashi!</i>

00:00:13.284 --> 00:00:17.121
Good <i>Morning Yamanashi Yamanashi!
Good morning, Yamanashi!</i>

00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:17.747
<i>Yamanashi!
Good morning, Yamanashi!</i>

00:00:18.373 --> 00:00:19.374
<i>Good morning.</i>

00:00:23.586 --> 00:00:25.421
There's a seat over here, Fukuda.

00:00:25.755 --> 00:00:28.883
Oh, so you're here again today?

00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:37.308
This year's cold is a real bugger to shake.

00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:42.397
Be mindful of any complications, okay?

00:00:43.565 --> 00:00:46.067
The shot should do the trick, mind.

00:00:46.276 --> 00:00:49.737
But just in case, I'll give you
a week's prescription.

00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:50.697
Yes, sir.

00:00:51.573 --> 00:00:53.783
Next, please. Mr. Kawasaki?

00:00:54.075 --> 00:00:56.202
- That's me.
- Thank you very much, doctor.

00:00:56.202 --> 00:00:58.162
You're welcome. Take care.

00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:00.331
Hello.

00:01:00.331 --> 00:01:01.791
So what's wrong with you?

00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:04.502
Seems I caught a cold.

00:01:05.503 --> 00:01:06.546
Take care.

00:01:22.895 --> 00:01:25.106
I hope the shot will help...

00:02:02.977 --> 00:02:08.566
The Stinkiest Weapon

00:02:16.282 --> 00:02:19.285
Oh, Mr. Tanaka. All better now?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.997
No, I still have a fever. I just don't
want to sit at home by myself.

00:02:23.373 --> 00:02:26.167
Besides, I don't have a
girl to take care of me.

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:27.460
Take care.

00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:52.276
You're gonna set off
the BioCon alarm, Nobuo.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.822
I got a shot at the clinic.

00:02:56.155 --> 00:02:59.784
Why don't you test out all our
over-the-counter cold medicines?

00:03:00.076 --> 00:03:01.828
Kill two birds with one stone.

00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:03.538
I have been trying them.

00:03:05.373 --> 00:03:08.334
Why not try that new medicine
we're developing, then?

00:03:08.751 --> 00:03:10.461
I saw a sample on the chief's desk.

00:03:11.045 --> 00:03:13.381
It should be good,
it's pre-market stuff.

00:03:13.381 --> 00:03:17.051
Oh, yeah.
Those blue pills in the red bottle.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.137
Two of those should work right away.

00:03:26.477 --> 00:03:30.398
<i>Attention, Mr. Okamura in the infirmary.</i>

00:03:30.648 --> 00:03:33.735
<i>You have a call on line three.</i>

00:03:39.323 --> 00:03:42.618
Excuse me, chief.
About these papers...

00:03:42.994 --> 00:03:43.661
Huh...?

00:03:45.455 --> 00:03:47.707
Oh, he's out.

00:04:01.721 --> 00:04:05.224
Red pills in a blue bottle...

00:04:06.517 --> 00:04:07.810
Are these them?

00:04:12.064 --> 00:04:14.358
There's a blue bottle...

00:04:16.527 --> 00:04:18.529
And red pills.

00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:31.918
Maybe just one?

00:04:34.587 --> 00:04:37.590
No way! You look so cool, Miki!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.802
Oh, I can do anything if I
just set my mind to it.

00:04:40.802 --> 00:04:42.512
That's so great!

00:04:42.887 --> 00:04:47.225
Sakiko, you should've come with us!
We had the best time!

00:04:49.602 --> 00:04:52.021
What's that smell?

00:04:54.398 --> 00:04:57.610
Oh, I smell it.
Maybe someone ate something bad?

00:04:57.985 --> 00:05:00.822
No, it's not like that. It smells good.

00:05:01.948 --> 00:05:03.950
Like perfume.

00:05:06.452 --> 00:05:08.287
Who did it?!

00:05:13.584 --> 00:05:16.546
Who? Who touched my red pills?

00:05:16.879 --> 00:05:18.923
Who came into my office?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.637
A little while ago, Nobuo-
I mean, Mr. Tanaka went in there.

00:05:24.846 --> 00:05:26.389
He took a sample of the new meds.

00:05:26.472 --> 00:05:27.306
He what?!

00:05:28.683 --> 00:05:30.601
Where is he now?

00:05:31.269 --> 00:05:33.187
He was just here a moment ago...

00:05:33.312 --> 00:05:35.231
Now! Where is he now?

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:37.942
Maybe he went home?

00:05:38.109 --> 00:05:40.862
H-H-H-Home?!

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.948
Why did you let him go? You idiot!

00:05:44.115 --> 00:05:46.367
This is your fault!
It's going to be your head!

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:51.581
Chief! Tanaka wasn't feeling well,
so he went to take a nap in reception.

00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:53.958
Huh? Are you sure?

00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:55.042
Yeah.

00:05:56.544 --> 00:05:59.547
Is something wrong with
that new fever medicine?

00:06:00.214 --> 00:06:02.717
Fever medicine?
Who the hell said it was that?

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:04.760
Then what was...?

00:06:10.933 --> 00:06:12.602
What's that smell?

00:07:06.447 --> 00:07:07.365
It's morning?

00:07:08.032 --> 00:07:09.742
Oh crap, it is.

00:07:11.077 --> 00:07:14.330
People should be coming in to work now.

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:16.707
Great.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.836
Why didn't somebody wake me?

00:07:38.896 --> 00:07:39.939
Sakiko?

00:07:45.111 --> 00:07:46.028
Sakiko!

00:07:48.197 --> 00:07:50.241
Somebody! Anybody!

00:07:50.449 --> 00:07:52.952
Somebody, help!

00:08:25.526 --> 00:08:28.696
Ambulance!
Gotta call an ambulance!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:37.038
Some kind of accident?

00:08:37.663 --> 00:08:41.250
But the alarm should have gone off!

00:08:45.129 --> 00:08:46.422
Same as yesterday...

00:08:47.631 --> 00:08:49.592
Hello? I need help!

00:08:49.759 --> 00:08:51.844
I need an ambulance out here, please!

00:08:58.184 --> 00:09:00.895
Ch... Chief?

00:09:09.028 --> 00:09:10.905
Ch-Chief!

00:09:10.905 --> 00:09:12.656
Master Power
Backup Power

00:09:14.992 --> 00:09:16.869
The BioCon alarm's turned off?

00:09:17.912 --> 00:09:20.790
Why? Did the chief turn it off?

00:09:37.014 --> 00:09:37.515
Accident Occurred

00:09:37.515 --> 00:09:38.224
<i>Accident Occurred
An accident has occurred.</i>

00:09:38.224 --> 00:09:38.933
<i>An</i> accident has occurred.

00:09:38.933 --> 00:09:39.391
<i>Accident Occurred
An accident has occurred.</i>

00:09:39.391 --> 00:09:39.850
<i>An</i> accident has occurred.

00:09:40.017 --> 00:09:40.518
<i>Please remain calm
and follow instructions.</i>

00:09:40.518 --> 00:09:41.060
Accident Occurred Please remain
calm and follow instructions.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.895
<i>Please remain calm
and follow instructions.</i>

00:09:42.895 --> 00:09:44.396
Accident Occurred

00:09:45.439 --> 00:09:48.818
An accident? I knew it! Oh, man!

00:09:49.193 --> 00:09:53.030
<i>- Give this line priority!
- Yeah! First priority!</i>

00:09:53.405 --> 00:09:54.615
<i>What happened, Omaeda?</i>

00:09:55.699 --> 00:09:56.992
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:09:57.201 --> 00:09:58.661
I'm, well, uh...

00:09:58.869 --> 00:10:01.664
<i>Where's Omaeda?
The guy in charge!</i>

00:10:01.664 --> 00:10:03.499
If you mean the chief,
he's right here.

00:10:09.505 --> 00:10:11.423
<i>What the hell? What's going on?</i>

00:10:11.799 --> 00:10:13.509
<i>What's Omaeda doing on the floor?</i>

00:10:13.801 --> 00:10:17.304
I don't know. It's not just
the chief, either, it's everyone.

00:10:17.346 --> 00:10:19.640
<i>What? Patch in the other monitors.</i>

00:10:21.559 --> 00:10:24.353
I think we had an accident or something.

00:10:25.062 --> 00:10:26.647
<i>- And who are you?
- Tanaka.</i>

00:10:26.981 --> 00:10:29.150
Nobuo Tanaka, Development Room 3.

00:10:29.358 --> 00:10:32.319
<i>How long? Tell me the exact
hour and minute this happened!</i>

00:10:32.528 --> 00:10:34.738
Well, it was like this
when I woke up.

00:10:34.864 --> 00:10:37.449
<i>What? But the alarm just went off!</i>

00:10:37.449 --> 00:10:40.661
- Well, the chief turned off the alarm-
- That's impossible!

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.205
<i>You don't know anything.
Wake up Omaeda!</i>

00:10:43.247 --> 00:10:46.041
He's unconscious,
just like everyone else.

00:10:46.834 --> 00:10:48.043
<i>I don't believe this...</i>

00:10:48.043 --> 00:10:51.630
I called an ambulance,
but they aren't here yet.

00:10:52.131 --> 00:10:54.258
<i>What? You called an ambulance?</i>

00:10:54.425 --> 00:10:55.968
Yes, and the police.

00:10:56.302 --> 00:10:57.136
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:10:57.511 --> 00:10:58.637
<i>Hold on.</i>

00:11:00.389 --> 00:11:02.349
<i>What? My God.</i>

00:11:04.685 --> 00:11:05.686
Yeah, <i>I</i> see.

00:11:08.772 --> 00:11:10.691
<i>- You said your name was Tanaka?
- Yes, sir.</i>

00:11:12.276 --> 00:11:13.819
<i>Listen to me very carefully.</i>

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.531
<i>I want you to find a certain
medicine and some papers.</i>

00:11:18.157 --> 00:11:22.036
<i>And I want you to bring them to me
at headquarters here in Tokyo.</i>

00:11:22.286 --> 00:11:25.623
<i>I'm Kyoichi Nirasaki, the head
of New Medicine Development.</i>

00:11:25.789 --> 00:11:28.918
<i>Don't give the medicine or
the papers to anyone but me.</i>

00:11:29.126 --> 00:11:30.961
What? Right now?

00:11:30.961 --> 00:11:36.926
<i>Yes! And if anyone asks you,
don't say you work for the company!</i>

00:11:37.218 --> 00:11:38.719
What are you saying?

00:11:39.053 --> 00:11:42.306
<i>This accident... no, we still
can't say that it was for sure...</i>

00:11:42.473 --> 00:11:44.475
<i>This likely involves that medicine...</i>

00:11:44.516 --> 00:11:48.312
<i>As it's one we were secretly
developing for the government!</i>

00:11:49.897 --> 00:11:51.315
Orders from the government?

00:11:51.649 --> 00:11:57.154
<i>Exactly. And that is why we
can't reveal that this happened, yet.</i>

00:11:58.322 --> 00:12:00.532
<i>You don't have much time, Tanaka.</i>

00:12:01.992 --> 00:12:05.079
<i>Get out of there
before the police come!</i>

00:12:05.454 --> 00:12:09.541
<i>We need the code number for the files
and a list of the project head staff.</i>

00:12:10.376 --> 00:12:13.379
<i>And of course, the medicine sample.</i>

00:12:17.132 --> 00:12:18.008
This bottle...

00:12:19.426 --> 00:12:21.136
It wasn't fever medicine?

00:12:21.804 --> 00:12:23.472
But I took some...

00:13:15.524 --> 00:13:17.526
What's going on here?

00:13:18.152 --> 00:13:20.821
Cherry blossoms and sunflowers
in bloom at the same time?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:43.427
Hey! Hey! What's wrong?

00:13:50.559 --> 00:13:51.643
Just like the others.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.221
East sector troops!
Can you deploy for evac ops?

00:15:14.351 --> 00:15:18.105
<i>Do you read me, Niigata? Niigata Base!</i>

00:15:29.116 --> 00:15:33.662
Kamata, president of Nishibashi Pharma,
and Head of Development, Nirasaki.

00:15:34.872 --> 00:15:37.624
You gentlemen mind telling me
what the hell's going on?

00:15:38.167 --> 00:15:40.919
We're live at the Sasago
Tunnel on the Chuoh Freeway.

00:15:40.961 --> 00:15:44.506
The westbound highway into
the Kofu Valley is completely shut off.

00:15:44.673 --> 00:15:49.595
Eastbound is jammed and traffic
is at a standstill from all the accidents.

00:15:50.053 --> 00:15:53.474
While increasing numbers of
refugees are leaving Katsunuma,

00:15:53.682 --> 00:15:57.603
communication with the
central valley remains out.

00:15:58.604 --> 00:16:03.567
As you can see, I'm wearing a gas mask,
but it isn't keeping the smell out!

00:16:04.067 --> 00:16:06.528
The question remains:
What's going on in the valley?

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.239
And what is this smell?

00:16:19.416 --> 00:16:21.084
Look at that!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:24.379
Can you see this, folks?

00:16:24.755 --> 00:16:25.547
Flowers!

00:16:25.964 --> 00:16:29.301
All of the Kofu Valley is
full of blooming flowers!

00:16:29.801 --> 00:16:33.931
It looks like all the plants
in the valley are in bloom!

00:16:34.139 --> 00:16:37.059
However, I can't see anything
moving down there.

00:16:45.692 --> 00:16:47.778
This is quite the sight, viewers!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.531
It's like hell in full bloom!

00:16:50.697 --> 00:16:53.325
I can't even estimate
the number of victims.

00:16:53.575 --> 00:16:54.785
- I see someone!
- What?

00:17:01.959 --> 00:17:04.253
A survivor! Unbelievable!

00:17:04.586 --> 00:17:05.712
Let's rescue him!

00:17:06.046 --> 00:17:10.217
The cops are warning against
flying below 300 meters.

00:17:10.425 --> 00:17:13.220
Human life comes first!
And we'll get some awards!

00:17:14.096 --> 00:17:15.514
Hey!

00:17:22.521 --> 00:17:24.523
Folks, this report defies death!

00:17:24.731 --> 00:17:26.441
A live televised rescue!

00:17:31.488 --> 00:17:33.198
Hey!

00:17:48.714 --> 00:17:51.008
Hey! Speak to me. Hey!

00:17:59.349 --> 00:18:01.476
Somebody, help me!

00:18:02.561 --> 00:18:06.231
I've never heard any reports
on any medical research like that!

00:18:06.398 --> 00:18:12.112
Well, the Minister handed down the order
to develop a bioweapon countermeasure.

00:18:12.154 --> 00:18:14.156
One for our peacekeeping dispatches.

00:18:14.489 --> 00:18:17.826
From that, we set up a top secret
research team internally.

00:18:18.201 --> 00:18:21.371
Are you saying you were ordered
to develop a weapon?

00:18:21.496 --> 00:18:23.999
Huh? No! It was a countermeasure!

00:18:24.207 --> 00:18:26.877
But you see, the
head of the team, Mr. Omaeda,

00:18:27.085 --> 00:18:31.673
accidentally discovered a potent
side-effect from one of the compounds.

00:18:31.965 --> 00:18:33.800
Potent? How potent?

00:18:34.134 --> 00:18:39.306
We're still in the midst of analyzing
the data left in the lab's computers.

00:18:39.514 --> 00:18:43.602
You'll know as soon as we do, sir.

00:18:44.853 --> 00:18:46.480
What about our Special Forces?

00:18:46.605 --> 00:18:48.315
How long have they been at the scene?

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:54.196
They reported a moment ago that they
were gathering info in the valley, but...

00:18:54.988 --> 00:18:56.573
"But"? Speak up, man!

00:18:56.907 --> 00:18:59.409
According to the sensors
we airdropped in,

00:18:59.576 --> 00:19:02.663
the center of the
contaminated area is moving.

00:19:03.038 --> 00:19:03.997
What?!

00:19:04.289 --> 00:19:08.794
I think the wind is carrying the
gas cloud created by the accident, sir!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.310
I'm hungry...

00:19:31.692 --> 00:19:35.821
We must find the cause and
develop a countermeasure quickly.

00:19:36.029 --> 00:19:40.951
One of the research center staff is on
his way to Tokyo to bring a sample.

00:19:41.243 --> 00:19:43.704
I believe he should be here soon.

00:19:44.705 --> 00:19:45.872
You have a sample?

00:19:46.081 --> 00:19:51.211
Yes, the young man who
reported this accident should have it.

00:19:51.503 --> 00:19:53.880
What do you mean?

00:19:55.549 --> 00:20:00.887
We wanted to keep the classified documents
and the sample safe from outsiders.

00:20:01.263 --> 00:20:03.473
You're saying there's
a survivor down there?

00:20:18.071 --> 00:20:21.283
The smell's getting strong.
The biochem gear isn't enough!

00:20:21.658 --> 00:20:24.077
The evac is complete!
Begin withdrawal!

00:20:24.286 --> 00:20:26.705
- Seal the road when everyone is back!
- Yes, sir.

00:20:26.913 --> 00:20:28.165
Captain, look!

00:20:34.713 --> 00:20:35.756
What the-?

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.766
All right, he'll be the last evacuee.

00:20:45.974 --> 00:20:47.642
- Rescue him!
- Yes, sir!

00:20:48.143 --> 00:20:51.104
Move out!
Get that stuff packed up ASAP!

00:20:51.688 --> 00:20:54.149
Hey! Are you okay?

00:20:54.316 --> 00:20:55.859
Yeah!

00:21:01.823 --> 00:21:02.699
What the...?

00:21:23.887 --> 00:21:27.265
He's the one.
He's making this smell!

00:21:28.892 --> 00:21:31.478
Withdraw! Everybody, withdraw!

00:21:32.062 --> 00:21:34.940
Huh? Are they
afraid of the cloud?!

00:21:35.148 --> 00:21:38.401
Hey, wait a minute!

00:21:40.529 --> 00:21:42.447
Hey!Hey!

00:21:58.922 --> 00:22:00.465
Wait!

00:22:11.893 --> 00:22:13.520
Shit.

00:22:14.145 --> 00:22:15.438
Hurry!

00:22:42.465 --> 00:22:43.967
Why is it following me?!

00:22:44.301 --> 00:22:47.721
Wait for me!

00:22:49.347 --> 00:22:52.392
Grandpa, hurry!
Nobuo's in big trouble!

00:22:52.934 --> 00:22:55.020
What's happened to Nobuo?

00:22:57.689 --> 00:22:59.733
<i>All contact with Kofu has been
cut off for about ten hours, now.</i>

00:22:59.733 --> 00:23:02.694
<i>All contact with Kofu has been out off for about
ten hours, now. Grandma!</i> I <i>brought Grandpa!</i>

00:23:02.694 --> 00:23:02.986
<i>As for the lone survivor,
we believe we've identified him.</i>

00:23:02.986 --> 00:23:04.571
As for the lone survivor, we believe
we've identified <i>him.</i> What's wrong?

00:23:04.571 --> 00:23:04.988
<i>As for the lone survivor,
we believe we've identified him.</i>

00:23:04.988 --> 00:23:09.743
<i>As for the lone survivor, we believe</i> we've <i>identified
him.</i> Dear, <i>it's Nobuo! Nobuo's in trouble, he is!</i>

00:23:11.202 --> 00:23:11.703
Hel-

00:23:11.828 --> 00:23:12.037
<i>This is Nobuo Tanaka of Nishibashi Pharma,
and his approximate age.</i>

00:23:12.037 --> 00:23:13.413
<i>This is Nobuo Tanaka of Nishibashi Pharma, and
his approximate age. Mr. Nobuo Tanaka (23)</i>

00:23:13.413 --> 00:23:15.123
<i>This is Nobuo Tanaka of Nishibashi Pharma,
and his approximate age.</i>

00:23:15.123 --> 00:23:18.543
<i>This is Nobuo Tanaka of Nishibashi Pharma, and his
approximate age. Oh, Nobuo!</i> What have <i>you done now?</i>

00:23:19.377 --> 00:23:21.796
Contaminated zone now
beyond Sasago Tunnel!

00:23:22.672 --> 00:23:26.134
I think we can conclude
that guy is the cause of all this.

00:23:26.551 --> 00:23:32.140
The report from our troops leading
evac at Sasago supports that idea.

00:23:36.686 --> 00:23:43.443
We've found there's discrepancies between
our analysis and the data collected on-site.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:47.322
I theorize that the substance
is mixing with other compounds, or...

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:52.202
Rather, a kind of reaction is
going on within his body.

00:23:52.494 --> 00:23:55.872
Assuming that Tanaka
took the sample, of course.

00:23:55.997 --> 00:23:58.500
Can you just put it simply for us?

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.001
Oh, of course...

00:24:01.086 --> 00:24:08.885
There's no doubt that Nobuo Tanaka's
body itself is creating the smell.

00:24:08.885 --> 00:24:12.847
I believe the smell is
produced with his sweat,

00:24:12.847 --> 00:24:16.935
in proportion to his emotions,
body movement, and metabolism.

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:19.521
So, what should we do?

00:24:20.146 --> 00:24:23.525
Well, we have to make sure he stays calm.

00:24:23.525 --> 00:24:27.529
At the same time, we'll need to
figure out how to feed him, and...

00:24:27.529 --> 00:24:28.488
In other words...

00:24:29.489 --> 00:24:32.534
You're saying it's better to kill him!

00:24:33.243 --> 00:24:34.953
I can't approve that.

00:24:35.745 --> 00:24:38.581
My country invested
in this research as well.

00:24:38.873 --> 00:24:42.210
The sample has to be caught alive.

00:24:42.919 --> 00:24:46.172
That's rich! You're the ones who
started the research to begin with!

00:24:46.339 --> 00:24:48.675
Who do you think should
take responsibility?

00:24:49.551 --> 00:24:53.680
We can't worry about that now!
We have a more important duty!

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:55.265
The protection of our people!

00:25:21.207 --> 00:25:25.253
Do you see the long tail
on that gas cloud, folks?

00:25:25.462 --> 00:25:27.047
The stench is incredible!

00:25:27.547 --> 00:25:30.717
We can hardly keep our eyes
open for more than a minute,

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:33.053
despite the altitude
and our gas masks!

00:25:33.303 --> 00:25:35.472
The cloud is making its way to Tokyo.

00:25:35.597 --> 00:25:38.141
It's likely to bring the
same devastation there!

00:25:44.481 --> 00:25:47.442
<i>Nobuo!</i>

00:25:49.569 --> 00:25:53.782
<i>Nobuo! Can you hear me, Nobuo?</i>

00:25:54.074 --> 00:25:55.241
Grandma?

00:25:55.617 --> 00:26:00.580
Don't go to Tokyo!
Go <i>back</i> to the mountains!

00:26:00.705 --> 00:26:04.334
<i>I don't understand why,
but people will be in danger!</i>

00:26:04.584 --> 00:26:07.462
<i>Do you hear me, Nobuo?
Don't go to Tokyo!</i>

00:26:07.462 --> 00:26:09.297
Why is Grandma here?

00:26:10.507 --> 00:26:13.593
Hurry! Shoot him before
he's hidden by the gas!

00:26:21.059 --> 00:26:22.352
What was that?

00:26:22.644 --> 00:26:24.104
<i>Hey, what are you doing?</i>

00:26:24.187 --> 00:26:28.024
Are you trying to kill my grandson?
Hey! Let me go!

00:26:28.233 --> 00:26:29.818
What are you doing? Shoot him!

00:26:30.360 --> 00:26:33.571
Damn! The gas.
My eyes are watering!

00:26:33.613 --> 00:26:35.573
We can't stay at this altitude!

00:26:35.990 --> 00:26:37.450
- I'm taking us up!
- Shit!

00:26:38.910 --> 00:26:39.994
Grandma!

00:26:43.373 --> 00:26:45.083
Grandma!

00:26:47.585 --> 00:26:48.795
Grandma!

00:26:58.346 --> 00:26:59.889
What was-?

00:27:14.946 --> 00:27:17.740
Message in from attack troops:
Commencing attack!

00:27:17.949 --> 00:27:20.827
- Sci Ops contact imminent.
- Reading radio interference.

00:27:32.630 --> 00:27:35.383
Target is at the rear left,
approaching the bridge!

00:27:35.592 --> 00:27:39.137
We'll hit him and then
bug out as fast as we can!

00:27:40.597 --> 00:27:44.434
- He's out! I see the target!
- All right! Get set to attack!

00:27:44.642 --> 00:27:48.605
- I lost the target in the cloud!
- Forget it! Just blast the area!

00:27:49.939 --> 00:27:50.690
Fire!

00:27:55.570 --> 00:27:59.032
- Idiot! What are you shooting at?
- The precision sight isn't working!

00:27:59.532 --> 00:28:00.366
What?

00:28:01.618 --> 00:28:04.746
- What's wrong?
- The engine!

00:28:08.958 --> 00:28:12.712
- Idiot! Why are we stopping?
- I don't know!

00:28:20.929 --> 00:28:23.806
- Where are our tanks?
- The target is still moving.

00:28:24.015 --> 00:28:25.433
Why can't they stop him?

00:28:58.675 --> 00:29:00.551
He just now passed Uenohara.

00:29:02.011 --> 00:29:04.973
- No response from attack squad!
- No contact with Atsugi Base!

00:29:05.014 --> 00:29:06.140
We can't do anything!

00:29:06.349 --> 00:29:09.602
The stink gas is scrambling the
integrated circuits in our weapons!

00:29:09.811 --> 00:29:12.105
Call the commander
of the north-side troops!

00:29:12.313 --> 00:29:14.399
Call the prime minister! Hurry!

00:29:14.983 --> 00:29:16.693
Send evacuation orders to Tokyo!

00:29:16.859 --> 00:29:20.488
He's still alive.
Moving eastbound at 60 kph!

00:29:54.897 --> 00:29:57.317
What? What's wrong?

00:30:05.450 --> 00:30:06.617
It's broken?

00:30:07.869 --> 00:30:10.538
<i>The airport is now over crowd capacity.</i>

00:30:10.747 --> 00:30:13.708
<i>Please follow orders.</i>

00:30:28.639 --> 00:30:32.852
In two hours, the prime minister will
issue a statement, asking the world for help.

00:30:33.436 --> 00:30:36.731
The U.N. will then dispatch
peacekeeping forces.

00:30:37.106 --> 00:30:39.734
They'll turn Tokyo into a sea of fire.

00:30:39.942 --> 00:30:43.196
It's useless to argue over who's
responsible for this disaster.

00:30:43.863 --> 00:30:47.200
You two should escape.
I'm sure you have families.

00:30:49.619 --> 00:30:52.372
But, commander,
Your Excellency, what about you?

00:30:55.458 --> 00:30:57.001
You called me "Your Excellency."

00:31:02.715 --> 00:31:04.509
Everything is prepared, sir.

00:31:04.717 --> 00:31:06.427
Very well. Let's pull out.

00:31:06.969 --> 00:31:08.096
Aye, aye, sir!

00:31:11.599 --> 00:31:13.726
You!

00:31:16.229 --> 00:31:19.357
Tell me! Tell me what you're up to!

00:31:37.417 --> 00:31:39.752
NASA's latest space suit?

00:31:40.128 --> 00:31:42.422
Yes! Though it's still a prototype.

00:31:42.463 --> 00:31:45.091
Even so, it'll ignore
electromagnetic radiation.

00:31:45.133 --> 00:31:47.635
And its armor is impenetrable!

00:31:47.844 --> 00:31:50.513
Even a hit from a
trench mortar couldn't stop it.

00:31:50.972 --> 00:31:54.142
So you're really going to
try and capture him alive?

00:31:54.851 --> 00:31:57.645
Japan's prime minister has given up.

00:31:57.812 --> 00:31:59.689
Surely there's no harm in trying?

00:32:01.190 --> 00:32:01.983
Dammit!

00:32:02.692 --> 00:32:05.903
Relay this to our forces:
Stop him at Mt. Takao at all costs!

00:32:05.945 --> 00:32:06.487
Yes, sir!

00:32:24.672 --> 00:32:27.550
I bet they're still looking for me...

00:32:32.513 --> 00:32:33.556
Really?

00:32:39.687 --> 00:32:42.982
This whole thing's
turned into a real pain.

00:32:43.941 --> 00:32:48.237
And to top it off, I feel hungry
all the time for some reason...

00:33:02.543 --> 00:33:05.630
Good, we did it!
Switch it on, full power!

00:33:24.524 --> 00:33:26.984
Yeah! Get that air moving!

00:33:27.193 --> 00:33:30.863
Freeze him like a
Sapporo Snow Festival sculpture!

00:33:34.242 --> 00:33:35.743
What's going on?

00:33:37.078 --> 00:33:38.454
What now?

00:33:39.497 --> 00:33:40.873
Nobody told me about this!

00:33:58.516 --> 00:34:01.018
Who are you?
What are you doing here?

00:34:02.562 --> 00:34:05.773
- You can't just come in here and-
- Orders, sir.

00:34:07.275 --> 00:34:07.942
Hey!

00:34:09.193 --> 00:34:11.988
Captain! The gas is getting stronger.
It's dangerous!

00:34:12.405 --> 00:34:13.364
What?

00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:18.786
Damn! Why's it taking so long
to get that liquid nitrogen?

00:34:25.418 --> 00:34:26.335
Hey, don't!

00:34:27.003 --> 00:34:30.214
We can't get him any more
worked up, he's scared enough!

00:34:30.548 --> 00:34:33.426
We're even starting to get
electrical discharge inside the cloud!

00:34:33.759 --> 00:34:35.678
Wait for the nitrogen tanks to arrive!

00:34:35.845 --> 00:34:36.637
Hey!

00:34:40.558 --> 00:34:44.729
Fine, go on, then! I'll be here
to clean up after you're gone!

00:34:59.994 --> 00:35:02.955
All right!
This side isn't sealed off yet!

00:35:03.164 --> 00:35:04.373
I can get out!

00:36:39.635 --> 00:36:42.138
Everyone out! Let's go!

00:36:59.488 --> 00:37:01.991
It's been 30 minutes
since our last contact.

00:37:02.199 --> 00:37:03.909
Have you heard anything yet?

00:37:08.664 --> 00:37:10.624
Th-This reading...!

00:37:10.916 --> 00:37:12.334
The density is decreasing.

00:37:12.543 --> 00:37:15.045
What? Are you sure, Nirasaki?

00:37:15.129 --> 00:37:19.759
Yes, sir. This is the highest point.
See? And now it's like this!

00:37:22.636 --> 00:37:24.180
We've got comms back!

00:37:24.388 --> 00:37:27.183
We've got video from the
chopper too. Putting it on-screen.

00:37:50.039 --> 00:37:52.333
Great! The Yanks are okay!

00:37:53.042 --> 00:37:54.752
Now let's bury that damn skunk!

00:37:55.044 --> 00:37:55.753
Yes, sir!

00:38:11.352 --> 00:38:15.815
Yes, somehow we managed.
We were able to save Japan.

00:38:16.690 --> 00:38:20.986
I see. The emperor didn't get on the plane.

00:38:21.445 --> 00:38:24.240
I'm glad we could
defeat that man,

00:38:24.448 --> 00:38:28.077
without making the emperor's
bravery all for nothing. Right.

00:38:31.372 --> 00:38:32.540
I see the space suit!

00:38:33.290 --> 00:38:35.543
The American soldier's back!

00:39:10.703 --> 00:39:11.453
Oh, the papers...

00:39:12.288 --> 00:39:13.789
Uh, thank you.

00:39:24.592 --> 00:39:26.802
Hello, Mr. Nirasaki.

00:39:29.513 --> 00:39:31.098
I'm glad I finally get to meet you.

00:39:31.223 --> 00:39:33.642
I was worried about where
they were taking me.

00:39:34.018 --> 00:39:36.604
I really thought
I wasn't going to make it.

00:39:37.855 --> 00:39:40.107
Hold on. Let me get out of this thing.

00:39:54.747 --> 00:39:55.873
What a stink!
